NAME
    usermod - modify a user account (root only)

SYNOPSIS
    usermod <user> -g <group|gid>

DESCRIPTION
    Changes a user's PRIMARY group in /etc/passwd. ROOT ONLY. The group may be a
    name (resolved via /etc/group) or a numeric gid. This is the "assign a user
    to a group" operation in the primary-gid model - a task carries one
    kernel-owned gid, so the primary group IS the passwd gid field.

    The account's uid, home, and password are preserved; only the gid changes.
    Full supplementary-group membership (a user in several groups at once) is a
    later step that needs the kernel identity to carry a group list.

EXAMPLES
    # groupadd staff
    # usermod user -g staff
    usermod: updated user

SEE ALSO
    useradd, groupadd, passwd, id
